hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24038","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, narrated to me Mahmud ibn Labid, that he retained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and retained a mouthful that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat from a bucket that was in their house."
"24039","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, he said: The swords of the Muslims clashed against al-Yaman, the father of Hudhayfah, on the day of Uhud, not knowing him, so they killed him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to pay his blood-money, but Hudhayfah gave his blood-money as charity to the Muslims."
"24040","Narrated to us Yazid, informed to us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Mahmud ibn Labid, he said: When Diversion in increase was revealed, he recited it until he reached: You will surely be asked that day about bliss. They said: O Messenger of Allah, about which bliss will we be asked, when they are only the two black ones, water and dates, and our swords are on our necks, and the enemy is present? About which bliss will we be asked? He said: That will be."
"24041","Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud, informed to us Ismail ibn Jafar, informed to me Amr, from Asim, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah loves a people, He tries them. So whoever is patient, for him is patience, and whoever panics, for him is panic."
